\par \par Article F-6 - Special requirements for quenched and tempered ferritic steels
_\par The material & is listed in Table AQT-1 and therefore \par the special requirements
of this article shall apply. Here Para. AF-605 is considered.\par 
\par AF-605 {\b Requirements for Heat Treatment After Forming}
\par Final center line radius             R{\sub f\tab }=
\par Plate thickness                      t\tab =
\par % extreme fiber elongation       75t/R{\sub f\tab }=
\par % extreme fiber elongation       50t/R{\sub f\tab }=
\par The extreme fiber elongation is <= 5%: the piece shall be requenched and tempered\par only in case of hot forming (AF-605 (b)).\par 
\par The extreme fiber elongation is > 5%: either case (a) or (b) shall apply:
\par    (a) in case of cold forming the piece shall be heat treated per AF-630.1
\par    (b) in case of hot forming the piece shall be requenched and tempered.\par 
